course: dictionary
lesson: 8363
title: Rouge: red, make-up and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word rouge comes from French, where it means red. Look at «une pomme rouge»: it means «a red apple». In French the colour word usually comes after the noun.
explain: In English, rouge is an older word for a red or pink powder or cream put on the cheeks. Today people usually say blusher or blush. If a sentence is about the face, a play, or a make-up box, rouge probably means this.
explain: Rouge is also the word for red in the game of roulette. The context tells you which meaning fits: a French lesson, a colour list, a make-up bag, or a casino table.
fact: Rouge means red in French, and it sounds like «roozh».
fact: «Une pomme rouge» means «a red apple»; in French, colour words usually come after the noun.
fact: The French flag is bleu, blanc, rouge: «blue, white, red» from the flagpole.
fact: «Un poisson rouge» means «a red fish», which is the French name for a goldfish.
fact: «Baton Rouge» means «red stick» and is a city in the USA; «Moulin Rouge» means «red windmill» and is a famous theatre in Paris.
exercise: «Une pomme rouge» is a red apple. In French, what does rouge mean? | Green | Blue | *Red | Yellow
exercise: Mia reads, «She put rouge on her cheeks for the school play.» What is rouge in this sentence? | A French flag | A red apple | *Blusher, a red or pink powder for the cheeks | A red fish
exercise: Which word is never used for ginger hair in French? | Roux | *Rouge | Rousse
test: In roulette, what colour does rouge mean? | Black | *Red | Green | White
test: Which place name means «red stick» in French? | Roulette | Paris | *Baton Rouge | Moulin Rouge
exam: The French word «rouge» can mean a colour, a make-up powder for the cheeks, or a roulette bet. Which meaning fits «une pomme rouge»? | *Red, the colour | Roulette | Blusher | Ginger hair
